product": "Apache", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-12-15", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99986, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-40684", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An authentication bypass using an alternate path or channel [CWE-288] in Fortinet FortiOS version 7.2.0 through 7.2.1 and 7.0.0 through 7.0.6, FortiProxy version 7.2.0 and version 7.0.0 through 7.0.6 and FortiSwitchManager version 7.2.0 and 7.0.0 allows an unauthenticated atttacker to perform operations on the administrative interface via specially crafted HTTP or HTTPS requests.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-40684", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-10-18T14:15:09.747000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94427, "updated_at": "2026-01-14T19:19:58.407000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An authentication bypass using an alternate path or channel [CWE-288] in Fortinet FortiOS version 7.2.0 through 7.2.1 and 7.0.0 through 7.0.6, FortiProxy version 7.2.0 and version 7.0.0 through 7.0.6 and FortiSwitchManager version 7.2.0 and 7.0.0 allows an unauthenticated atttacker to perform operations on the administrative interface via specially crafted HTTP or HTTPS requests.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Multiple Products", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-11-01", "kev_vuln_name": "Fortinet Multiple Products Authentication Bypass Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99983, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Fortinet"}, {"cve": "CVE-2024-3273", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, was found in D-Link DNS-320L, DNS-325, DNS-327L and DNS-340L up to 20240403. Affected is an unknown function of the file /cgi-bin/nas_sharing.cgi of the component HTTP GET Request Handler. The manipulation of the argument system leads to command injection. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-259284. NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer. NOTE: Vendor was contacted early and confirmed immediately that the product is end-of-life. It should be retired and replaced.", "cve_id": "CVE-2024-3273", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2024-04-04T01:15:50.387000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94425, "updated_at": "2025-10-30T19:53:04.050000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, was found in D-Link DNS-320L, DNS-325, DNS-327L and DNS-340L up to 20240403. Affected is an unknown function of the file /cgi-bin/nas_sharing.cgi of the component HTTP GET Request Handler. The manipulation of the argument system leads to command injection. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-259284. NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer. NOTE: Vendor was contacted early and confirmed immediately that the product is end-of-life. It should be retired and replaced.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Multiple NAS Devices", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2024-05-02", "kev_vuln_name": "D-Link Multiple NAS Devices Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99982, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "D-Link"}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-42013", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "It was found that the fix for CVE-2021-41773 in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was insufficient. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and Apache 2.4.50 and not earlier versions.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-42013", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-10-07T16:15:09.270000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.9441, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:36:49.387000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "It was found that the fix for CVE-2021-41773 in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was insufficient. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and Apache 2.4.50 and not earlier versions.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-11-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99979, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-0296", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "A vulnerability in the web interface of the Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause an affected device to reload unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition. It is also possible on certain software releases that the ASA will not reload, but an attacker could view sensitive system information without authentication by using directory traversal techniques. The vulnerability is due to lack of proper input validation of the HTTP URL. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request to an affected device. An exploit could allow the attacker to cause a DoS condition or unauthenticated disclosure of information. This vulnerability applies to IPv4 and IPv6 HTTP traffic. This vulnerability affects Cisco ASA Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software that is running on the following Cisco products: 3000 Series Industrial Security Appliance (ISA), ASA 1000V Cloud Firewall, ASA 5500 Series Adaptive Security Appliances, ASA 5500-X Series Next-Generation Firewalls, ASA Services Module for Cisco Catalyst 6500 Series Switches and Cisco 7600 Series Routers, Adaptive Security Virtual Appliance (ASAv), Firepower 2100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 4100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 9300 ASA Security Module, FTD Virtual (FTDv). Cisco Bug IDs: CSCvi16029.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-0296", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2018-06-07T12:29:00.403000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.94404, "updated_at": "2026-01-14T19:21:29.037000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "A vulnerability in the web interface of the Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause an affected device to reload unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition. It is also possible on certain software releases that the ASA will not reload, but an attacker could view sensitive system information without authentication by using directory traversal techniques. The vulnerability is due to lack of proper input validation of the HTTP URL. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request to an affected device. An exploit could allow the attacker to cause a DoS condition or unauthenticated disclosure of information. This vulnerability applies to IPv4 and IPv6 HTTP traffic. This vulnerability affects Cisco ASA Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software that is running on the following Cisco products: 3000 Series Industrial Security Appliance (ISA), ASA 1000V Cloud Firewall, ASA 5500 Series Adaptive Security Appliances, ASA 5500-X Series Next-Generation Firewalls, ASA Services Module for Cisco Catalyst 6500 Series Switches and Cisco 7600 Series Routers, Adaptive Security Virtual Appliance (ASAv), Firepower 2100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 4100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 9300 ASA Security Module, FTD Virtual (FTDv). Cisco Bug IDs: CSCvi16029.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA)", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) Denial-of-Service Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99978, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Cisco"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-36804", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "Multiple API endpoints in Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center 7.0.0 before version 7.6.17, from version 7.7.0 before version 7.17.10, from version 7.18.0 before version 7.21.4, from version 8.0.0 before version 8.0.3, from version 8.1.0 before version 8.1.3, and from version 8.2.0 before version 8.2.2, and from version 8.3.0 before 8.3.1 allows remote attackers with read permissions to a public or private Bitbucket repository to execute arbitrary code by sending a malicious HTTP request. This vulnerability was reported via our Bug Bounty Program by TheGrandPew.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-36804", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2022-08-25T06:15:09.077000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.944, "updated_at": "2025-10-24T13:37:44.367000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Multiple API endpoints in Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center 7.0.0 before version 7.6.17, from version 7.7.0 before version 7.17.10, from version 7.18.0 before version 7.21.4, from version 8.0.0 before version 8.0.3, from version 8.1.0 before version 8.1.3, and from version 8.2.0 before version 8.2.2, and from version 8.3.0 before 8.3.1 allows remote attackers with read permissions to a public or private Bitbucket repository to execute arbitrary code by sending a malicious HTTP request. This vulnerability was reported via our Bug Bounty Program by TheGrandPew.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Bitbucket Server and Data Center", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-10-21", "kev_vuln_name": "Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99977, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Atlassian"}, {"cve": "CVE-2023-44487", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "The HTTP/2 protocol allows a denial of service (server resource consumption) because request cancellation can reset many streams quickly, as exploited in the wild in August through October 2023.", "cve_id": "CVE-2023-44487", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2023-10-10T14:15:10.883000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.944, "updated_at": "2025-11-07T19:00:41.810000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "The HTTP/2 protocol allows a denial of service (server resource consumption) because request cancellation can reset many streams quickly, as exploited in the wild in August through October 2023.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP/2", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-10-31", "kev_vuln_name": "HTTP/2 Rapid Reset Attack Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99976, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "IETF"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-21587", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator product of Oracle E-Business Suite (component: Upload). Supported versions that are affected are 12.2.3-12.2.11. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-21587", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-10-18T21:15:10.960000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94397, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:09:18.740000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator product of Oracle E-Business Suite (component: Upload). Supported versions that are affected are 12.2.3-12.2.11. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "E-Business Suite", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-02-23", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle E-Business Suite Unspecified Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99975, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2019-16278", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Directory Traversal in the function http_verify in nostromo nhttpd through 1.9.6 allows an attacker to achieve remote code execution via a crafted HTTP request.", "cve_id": "CVE-2019-16278", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2019-10-14T17:15:09.427000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94393, "updated_at": "2025-11-06T14:57:37.237000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Directory Traversal in the function http_verify in nostromo nhttpd through 1.9.6 allows an attacker to achieve remote code execution via a crafted HTTP request.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "nhttpd", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2024-11-28", "kev_vuln_name": "Nostromo nhttpd Directory Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99974, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Nostromo"}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-3506", "cvss": 7.4, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0, 12.1.3.0, 12.2.1.0, 12.2.1.1 and 12.2.1.2. Difficult to exploit vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized creation, deletion or modification access to critical data or all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data as well as unauthorized access to critical data or complete access to all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 7.4 (Confidentiality and Integrity impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N).", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-3506", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2017-04-24T19:59:03.037000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.4, "epss_score": 0.94393, "updated_at": "2026-04-22T13:39:47.350000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0, 12.1.3.0, 12.2.1.0, 12.2.1.1 and 12.2.1.2. Difficult to exploit vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized creation, deletion or modification access to critical data or all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data as well as unauthorized access to critical data or complete access to all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 7.4 (Confidentiality and Integrity impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2024-06-24", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server OS Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99973, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-41773", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "A flaw was found in a change made to path normalization in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.49. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue is known to be exploited in the wild. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and not earlier versions. The fix in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was found to be incomplete, see CVE-2021-42013.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-41773", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-10-05T09:15:07.593000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94391, "updated_at": "2026-02-17T19:49:26.367000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A flaw was found in a change made to path normalization in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.49. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue is known to be exploited in the wild. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and not earlier versions. The fix in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was found to be incomplete, see CVE-2021-42013.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-11-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99973, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2002-1873", "cvss": 5.0, "desc": "Microsoft Exchange 2000, when used with Microsoft Remote Procedure Call (MSRPC), allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash or memory consumption) via malformed MSRPC calls.", "cve_id": "CVE-2002-1873", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2002-12-31T05:00:00+05:30", "cvss_score": 5.0, "epss_score": 0.15142, "updated_at": "2026-04-16T00:27:16.627000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:N/I:N/A:P", "description": "Microsoft Exchange 2000, when used with Microsoft Remote Procedure Call (MSRPC), allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash or memory consumption) via malformed MSRPC calls.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P4", "priority_score": 26.06, "epss_percentile": 0.94613, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-8407", "cvss": 5.5, "desc": "An information disclosure vulnerability exists when \\"Kernel Remote Procedure Call Provider\\" driver improperly initializes objects in memory, aka \\"MSRPC Information Disclosure Vulnerability.\\" This affects Windows 7, Windows Server 2012 R2, Windows RT 8.1, Windows Server 2008, Windows Server 2019, Windows Server 2012, Windows 8.1, Windows Server 2016, Windows Server 2008 R2, Windows 10, Windows 10 Servers.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-8407", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2018-11-14T01:29:00.287000+05:30", "cvss_score": 5.5, "epss_score": 0.01576, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T04:13:45.840000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.0/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "description": "An information disclosure vulnerability exists when \\"Kernel Remote Procedure Call Provider\\" driver improperly initializes objects in memory, aka \\"MSRPC Information Disclosure Vulnerability.\\" This affects Windows 7, Windows Server 2012 R2, Windows RT 8.1, Windows Server 2008, Windows Server 2019, Windows Server 2012, Windows 8.1, Windows Server 2016, Windows Server 2008 R2, Windows 10, Windows 10 Servers.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P4", "priority_score": 22.63, "epss_percentile": 0.8162, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2013-4688", "cvss": 7.8, "desc": "flowd in Juniper Junos 10.4 before 10.4R11 on SRX devices, when the MSRPC Application Layer Gateway (ALG) is enabled, allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (daemon crash) via crafted MSRPC requests, aka PR 772834.", "cve_id": "CVE-2013-4688", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2013-07-11T14:55:01.403000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.8, "epss_score": 0.00491, "updated_at": "2025-04-11T00:51:21.963000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:N/I:N/A:C", "description": "flowd in Juniper Junos 10.4 before 10.4R11 on SRX devices, when the MSRPC Application Layer Gateway (ALG) is enabled, allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (daemon crash) via crafted MSRPC requests, aka PR 772834.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 31.4, "epss_percentile": 0.6566, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2002-0597", "cvss": 5.0, "desc": "LANMAN service on Microsoft Windows 2000 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU/memory exhaustion) via a stream of malformed data to microsoft-ds port 445.", "cve_id": "CVE-2002-0597", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2002-06-18T04:00:00+05:30", "cvss_score": 5.0, "epss_score": 0.62388, "updated_at": "2026-04-16T00:27:16.627000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:N/I:N/A:P", "description": "LANMAN service on Microsoft Windows 2000 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU/memory exhaustion) via a stream of malformed data to microsoft-ds port 445.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 44.96, "epss_percentile": 0.98374, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-1000353", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Jenkins versions 2.56 and earlier as well as 2.46.1 LTS and earlier are vulnerable to an unauthenticated remote code execution. An unauthenticated remote code execution vulnerability allowed attackers to transfer a serialized Java `SignedObject` object to the Jenkins CLI, that would be deserialized using a new `ObjectInputStream`, bypassing the existing blacklist-based protection mechanism. We're fixing this issue by adding `SignedObject` to the blacklist. We're also backporting the new HTTP CLI protocol from Jenkins 2.54 to LTS 2.46.2, and deprecating the remoting-based (i.e. Java serialization) CLI protocol, disabling it by default.", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-1000353", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2018-01-29T17:29:00.193000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94482, "updated_at": "2025-11-05T19:24:40.943000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Jenkins versions 2.56 and earlier as well as 2.46.1 LTS and earlier are vulnerable to an unauthenticated remote code execution. An unauthenticated remote code execution vulnerability allowed attackers to transfer a serialized Java `SignedObject` object to the Jenkins CLI, that would be deserialized using a new `ObjectInputStream`, bypassing the existing blacklist-based protection mechanism. We're fixing this issue by adding `SignedObject` to the blacklist. We're also backporting the new HTTP CLI protocol from Jenkins 2.54 to LTS 2.46.2, and deprecating the remoting-based (i.e. Java serialization) CLI protocol, disabling it by default.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Jenkins", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2025-10-23", "kev_vuln_name": "Jenkins Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99999, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Jenkins"}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-13379", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory (\\"Path Traversal\\") in Fortinet FortiOS 6.0.0 to 6.0.4, 5.6.3 to 5.6.7 and 5.4.6 to 5.4.12 and FortiProxy 2.0.0, 1.2.0 to 1.2.8, 1.1.0 to 1.1.6, 1.0.0 to 1.0.7 under SSL VPN web portal allows an unauthenticated attacker to download system files via special crafted HTTP resource requests.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-13379", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2019-06-04T21:29:00.233000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94473, "updated_at": "2025-10-24T12:53:03.100000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory (\\"Path Traversal\\") in Fortinet FortiOS 6.0.0 to 6.0.4, 5.6.3 to 5.6.7 and 5.4.6 to 5.4.12 and FortiProxy 2.0.0, 1.2.0 to 1.2.8, 1.1.0 to 1.1.6, 1.0.0 to 1.0.7 under SSL VPN web portal allows an unauthenticated attacker to download system files via special crafted HTTP resource requests.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "FortiOS", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Fortinet FortiOS SSL VPN Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99999, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Fortinet"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-46169", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Cacti is an open source platform which provides a robust and extensible operational monitoring and fault management framework for users. In affected versions a command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary code on a server running Cacti, if a specific data source was selected for any monitored device. The vulnerability resides in the `remote_agent.php` file. This file can be accessed without authentication. This function retrieves the IP address of the client via `get_client_addr` and resolves this IP address to the corresponding hostname via `gethostbyaddr`. After this, it is verified that an entry within the `poller` table exists, where the hostname corresponds to the resolved hostname. If such an entry was found, the function returns `true` and the client is authorized. This authorization can be bypassed due to the implementation of the `get_client_addr` function. The function is defined in the file `lib/functions.php` and checks serval `$_SERVER` variables to determine the IP address of the client. The variables beginning with `HTTP_` can be arbitrarily set by an attacker. Since there is a default entry in the `poller` table with the hostname of the server running Cacti, an attacker can bypass the authentication e.g. by providing the header `Forwarded-For: <TARGETIP>`. This way the function `get_client_addr` returns the IP address of the server running Cacti. The following call to `gethostbyaddr` will resolve this IP address to the hostname of the server, which will pass the `poller` hostname check because of the default entry. After the authorization of the `remote_agent.php` file is bypassed, an attacker can trigger different actions. One of these actions is called `polldata`. The called function `poll_for_data` retrieves a few request parameters and loads the corresponding `poller_item` entries from the database. If the `action` of a `poller_item` equals `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`, the function `proc_open` is used to execute a PHP script. The attacker-controlled parameter `$poller_id` is retrieved via the function `get_nfilter_request_var`, which allows arbitrary strings. This variable is later inserted into the string passed to `proc_open`, which leads to a command injection vulnerability. By e.g. providing the `poller_id=;id` the `id` command is executed. In order to reach the vulnerable call, the attacker must provide a `host_id` and `local_data_id`, where the `action` of the corresponding `poller_item` is set to `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`. Both of these ids (`host_id` and `local_data_id`) can easily be bruteforced. The only requirement is that a `poller_item` with an `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` action exists. This is very likely on a productive instance because this action is added by some predefined templates like `Device - Uptime` or `Device - Polling Time`.\\n\\nThis command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary commands if a `poller_item` with the `action` type `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` (`2`) is configured. The authorization bypass should be prevented by not allowing an attacker to make `get_client_addr` (file `lib/functions.php`) return an arbitrary IP address. This could be done by not honoring the `HTTP_...` `$_SERVER` variables. If these should be kept for compatibility reasons it should at least be prevented to fake the IP address of the server running Cacti. This vulnerability has been addressed in both the 1.2.x and 1.3.x release branches with `1.2.23` being the first release containing the patch.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-46169", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-12-05T21:15:10.527000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94469, "updated_at": "2025-10-24T14:47:01.117000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Cacti is an open source platform which provides a robust and extensible operational monitoring and fault management framework for users. In affected versions a command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary code on a server running Cacti, if a specific data source was selected for any monitored device. The vulnerability resides in the `remote_agent.php` file. This file can be accessed without authentication. This function retrieves the IP address of the client via `get_client_addr` and resolves this IP address to the corresponding hostname via `gethostbyaddr`. After this, it is verified that an entry within the `poller` table exists, where the hostname corresponds to the resolved hostname. If such an entry was found, the function returns `true` and the client is authorized. This authorization can be bypassed due to the implementation of the `get_client_addr` function. The function is defined in the file `lib/functions.php` and checks serval `$_SERVER` variables to determine the IP address of the client. The variables beginning with `HTTP_` can be arbitrarily set by an attacker. Since there is a default entry in the `poller` table with the hostname of the server running Cacti, an attacker can bypass the authentication e.g. by providing the header `Forwarded-For: <TARGETIP>`. This way the function `get_client_addr` returns the IP address of the server running Cacti. The following call to `gethostbyaddr` will resolve this IP address to the hostname of the server, which will pass the `poller` hostname check because of the default entry. After the authorization of the `remote_agent.php` file is bypassed, an attacker can trigger different actions. One of these actions is called `polldata`. The called function `poll_for_data` retrieves a few request parameters and loads the corresponding `poller_item` entries from the database. If the `action` of a `poller_item` equals `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`, the function `proc_open` is used to execute a PHP script. The attacker-controlled parameter `$poller_id` is retrieved via the function `get_nfilter_request_var`, which allows arbitrary strings. This variable is later inserted into the string passed to `proc_open`, which leads to a command injection vulnerability. By e.g. providing the `poller_id=;id` the `id` command is executed. In order to reach the vulnerable call, the attacker must provide a `host_id` and `local_data_id`, where the `action` of the corresponding `poller_item` is set to `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`. Both of these ids (`host_id` and `local_data_id`) can easily be bruteforced. The only requirement is that a `poller_item` with an `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` action exists. This is very likely on a productive instance because this action is added by some predefined templates like `Device - Uptime` or `Device - Polling Time`.\\n\\nThis command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary commands if a `poller_item` with the `action` type `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` (`2`) is configured. The authorization bypass should be prevented by not allowing an attacker to make `get_client_addr` (file `lib/functions.php`) return an arbitrary IP address. This could be done by not honoring the `HTTP_...` `$_SERVER` variables. If these should be kept for compatibility reasons it should at least be prevented to fake the IP address of the server running Cacti. This vulnerability has been addressed in both the 1.2.x and 1.3.x release branches with `1.2.23` being the first release containing the patch.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Cacti", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-03-09", "kev_vuln_name": "Cacti Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99998, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Cacti"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-1938", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "When using the Apache JServ Protocol (AJP), care must be taken when trusting incoming connections to Apache Tomcat. Tomcat treats AJP connections as having higher trust than, for example, a similar HTTP connection. If such connections are available to an attacker, they can be exploited in ways that may be surprising. In Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0.30, 8.5.0 to 8.5.50 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.99, Tomcat shipped with an AJP Connector enabled by default that listened on all configured IP addresses. It was expected (and recommended in the security guide) that this Connector would be disabled if not required. This vulnerability report identified a mechanism that allowed: - returning arbitrary files from anywhere in the web application - processing any file in the web application as a JSP Further, if the web application allowed file upload and stored those files within the web application (or the attacker was able to control the content of the web application by some other means) then this, along with the ability to process a file as a JSP, made remote code execution possible. It is important to note that mitigation is only required if an AJP port is accessible to untrusted users. Users wishing to take a defence-in-depth approach and block the vector that permits returning arbitrary files and execution as JSP may upgrade to Apache Tomcat 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later. A number of changes were made to the default AJP Connector configuration in 9.0.31 to harden the default configuration. It is likely that users upgrading to 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later will need to make small changes to their configurations.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-1938", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-02-24T22:15:12.057000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94469, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:37:12.387000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "When using the Apache JServ Protocol (AJP), care must be taken when trusting incoming connections to Apache Tomcat. Tomcat treats AJP connections as having higher trust than, for example, a similar HTTP connection. If such connections are available to an attacker, they can be exploited in ways that may be surprising. In Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0.30, 8.5.0 to 8.5.50 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.99, Tomcat shipped with an AJP Connector enabled by default that listened on all configured IP addresses. It was expected (and recommended in the security guide) that this Connector would be disabled if not required. This vulnerability report identified a mechanism that allowed: - returning arbitrary files from anywhere in the web application - processing any file in the web application as a JSP Further, if the web application allowed file upload and stored those files within the web application (or the attacker was able to control the content of the web application by some other means) then this, along with the ability to process a file as a JSP, made remote code execution possible. It is important to note that mitigation is only required if an AJP port is accessible to untrusted users. Users wishing to take a defence-in-depth approach and block the vector that permits returning arbitrary files and execution as JSP may upgrade to Apache Tomcat 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later. A number of changes were made to the default AJP Connector configuration in 9.0.31 to harden the default configuration. It is likely that users upgrading to 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later will need to make small changes to their configurations.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Tomcat", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-03-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache Tomcat Improper Privilege Management Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99997, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2019-2725", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0 and 12.1.3.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2019-2725", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2019-04-26T19:29:00.463000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94468, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:08:18.543000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0 and 12.1.3.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-07-10", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server, Injection", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99997, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-14882", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-14882", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-10-21T15:15:25.407000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94454, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:09:11.960000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99992, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-3452", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "A vulnerability in the web services interface of Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to conduct directory traversal attacks and read sensitive files on a targeted system. The vulnerability is due to a lack of proper input validation of URLs in HTTP requests processed by an affected device. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request containing directory traversal character sequences to an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to view arbitrary files within the web services file system on the targeted device. The web services file system is enabled when the affected device is configured with either WebVPN or AnyConnect features. This vulnerability cannot be used to obtain access to ASA or FTD system files or underlying operating system (OS) files.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-3452", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-07-22T20:15:11.970000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.94452, "updated_at": "2025-10-28T13:54:01.140000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "description": "A vulnerability in the web services interface of Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to conduct directory traversal attacks and read sensitive files on a targeted system. The vulnerability is due to a lack of proper input validation of URLs in HTTP requests processed by an affected device. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request containing directory traversal character sequences to an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to view arbitrary files within the web services file system on the targeted device. The web services file system is enabled when the affected device is configured with either WebVPN or AnyConnect features. This vulnerability cannot be used to obtain access to ASA or FTD system files or underlying operating system (OS) files.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) and Firepower Threat Defense (FTD)", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Cisco ASA and FTD Read-Only Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99992, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Cisco"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-14883", "cvss": 7.2, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows high privileged attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 7.2 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-14883", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-10-21T15:15:25.483000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.2, "epss_score": 0.94439, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:09:08.300000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows high privileged attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 7.2 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server Unspecified Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.9999, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-14750", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-14750", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-11-02T21:15:24.493000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94438, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:08:31.047000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99988, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-40438", "cvss": 9.0, "desc": "A crafted request uri-path can cause mod_proxy to forward the request to an origin server choosen by the remote user. This issue affects Apache HTTP Server 2.4.48 and earlier.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-40438", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-09-16T15:15:07.633000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.0, "epss_score": 0.94432, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:37:06.747000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A crafted request uri-path can cause mod_proxy to forward the request to an origin server choosen by the remote user. This issue affects Apache HTTP Server 2.4.48 and earlier.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Apache", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-12-15", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99986, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-40684", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An authentication bypass using an alternate path or channel [CWE-288] in Fortinet FortiOS version 7.2.0 through 7.2.1 and 7.0.0 through 7.0.6, FortiProxy version 7.2.0 and version 7.0.0 through 7.0.6 and FortiSwitchManager version 7.2.0 and 7.0.0 allows an unauthenticated atttacker to perform operations on the administrative interface via specially crafted HTTP or HTTPS requests.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-40684", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-10-18T14:15:09.747000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94427, "updated_at": "2026-01-14T19:19:58.407000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An authentication bypass using an alternate path or channel [CWE-288] in Fortinet FortiOS version 7.2.0 through 7.2.1 and 7.0.0 through 7.0.6, FortiProxy version 7.2.0 and version 7.0.0 through 7.0.6 and FortiSwitchManager version 7.2.0 and 7.0.0 allows an unauthenticated atttacker to perform operations on the administrative interface via specially crafted HTTP or HTTPS requests.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Multiple Products", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-11-01", "kev_vuln_name": "Fortinet Multiple Products Authentication Bypass Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99983, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Fortinet"}, {"cve": "CVE-2024-3273", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, was found in D-Link DNS-320L, DNS-325, DNS-327L and DNS-340L up to 20240403. Affected is an unknown function of the file /cgi-bin/nas_sharing.cgi of the component HTTP GET Request Handler. The manipulation of the argument system leads to command injection. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-259284. NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer. NOTE: Vendor was contacted early and confirmed immediately that the product is end-of-life. It should be retired and replaced.", "cve_id": "CVE-2024-3273", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2024-04-04T01:15:50.387000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94425, "updated_at": "2025-10-30T19:53:04.050000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, was found in D-Link DNS-320L, DNS-325, DNS-327L and DNS-340L up to 20240403. Affected is an unknown function of the file /cgi-bin/nas_sharing.cgi of the component HTTP GET Request Handler. The manipulation of the argument system leads to command injection. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-259284. NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer. NOTE: Vendor was contacted early and confirmed immediately that the product is end-of-life. It should be retired and replaced.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Multiple NAS Devices", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2024-05-02", "kev_vuln_name": "D-Link Multiple NAS Devices Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99982, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "D-Link"}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-42013", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "It was found that the fix for CVE-2021-41773 in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was insufficient. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and Apache 2.4.50 and not earlier versions.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-42013", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-10-07T16:15:09.270000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.9441, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:36:49.387000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "It was found that the fix for CVE-2021-41773 in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was insufficient. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and Apache 2.4.50 and not earlier versions.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-11-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99979, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-0296", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "A vulnerability in the web interface of the Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause an affected device to reload unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition. It is also possible on certain software releases that the ASA will not reload, but an attacker could view sensitive system information without authentication by using directory traversal techniques. The vulnerability is due to lack of proper input validation of the HTTP URL. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request to an affected device. An exploit could allow the attacker to cause a DoS condition or unauthenticated disclosure of information. This vulnerability applies to IPv4 and IPv6 HTTP traffic. This vulnerability affects Cisco ASA Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software that is running on the following Cisco products: 3000 Series Industrial Security Appliance (ISA), ASA 1000V Cloud Firewall, ASA 5500 Series Adaptive Security Appliances, ASA 5500-X Series Next-Generation Firewalls, ASA Services Module for Cisco Catalyst 6500 Series Switches and Cisco 7600 Series Routers, Adaptive Security Virtual Appliance (ASAv), Firepower 2100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 4100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 9300 ASA Security Module, FTD Virtual (FTDv). Cisco Bug IDs: CSCvi16029.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-0296", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2018-06-07T12:29:00.403000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.94404, "updated_at": "2026-01-14T19:21:29.037000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "A vulnerability in the web interface of the Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause an affected device to reload unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition. It is also possible on certain software releases that the ASA will not reload, but an attacker could view sensitive system information without authentication by using directory traversal techniques. The vulnerability is due to lack of proper input validation of the HTTP URL. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request to an affected device. An exploit could allow the attacker to cause a DoS condition or unauthenticated disclosure of information. This vulnerability applies to IPv4 and IPv6 HTTP traffic. This vulnerability affects Cisco ASA Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software that is running on the following Cisco products: 3000 Series Industrial Security Appliance (ISA), ASA 1000V Cloud Firewall, ASA 5500 Series Adaptive Security Appliances, ASA 5500-X Series Next-Generation Firewalls, ASA Services Module for Cisco Catalyst 6500 Series Switches and Cisco 7600 Series Routers, Adaptive Security Virtual Appliance (ASAv), Firepower 2100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 4100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 9300 ASA Security Module, FTD Virtual (FTDv). Cisco Bug IDs: CSCvi16029.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA)", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) Denial-of-Service Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99978, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Cisco"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-36804", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "Multiple API endpoints in Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center 7.0.0 before version 7.6.17, from version 7.7.0 before version 7.17.10, from version 7.18.0 before version 7.21.4, from version 8.0.0 before version 8.0.3, from version 8.1.0 before version 8.1.3, and from version 8.2.0 before version 8.2.2, and from version 8.3.0 before 8.3.1 allows remote attackers with read permissions to a public or private Bitbucket repository to execute arbitrary code by sending a malicious HTTP request. This vulnerability was reported via our Bug Bounty Program by TheGrandPew.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-36804", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2022-08-25T06:15:09.077000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.944, "updated_at": "2025-10-24T13:37:44.367000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Multiple API endpoints in Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center 7.0.0 before version 7.6.17, from version 7.7.0 before version 7.17.10, from version 7.18.0 before version 7.21.4, from version 8.0.0 before version 8.0.3, from version 8.1.0 before version 8.1.3, and from version 8.2.0 before version 8.2.2, and from version 8.3.0 before 8.3.1 allows remote attackers with read permissions to a public or private Bitbucket repository to execute arbitrary code by sending a malicious HTTP request. This vulnerability was reported via our Bug Bounty Program by TheGrandPew.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Bitbucket Server and Data Center", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-10-21", "kev_vuln_name": "Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99977, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Atlassian"}, {"cve": "CVE-2023-44487", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "The HTTP/2 protocol allows a denial of service (server resource consumption) because request cancellation can reset many streams quickly, as exploited in the wild in August through October 2023.", "cve_id": "CVE-2023-44487", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2023-10-10T14:15:10.883000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.944, "updated_at": "2025-11-07T19:00:41.810000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "The HTTP/2 protocol allows a denial of service (server resource consumption) because request cancellation can reset many streams quickly, as exploited in the wild in August through October 2023.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP/2", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-10-31", "kev_vuln_name": "HTTP/2 Rapid Reset Attack Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99976, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "IETF"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-21587", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator product of Oracle E-Business Suite (component: Upload). Supported versions that are affected are 12.2.3-12.2.11. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-21587", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-10-18T21:15:10.960000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94397, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:09:18.740000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator product of Oracle E-Business Suite (component: Upload). Supported versions that are affected are 12.2.3-12.2.11. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle Web Applications Desktop Integrator. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "E-Business Suite", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-02-23", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle E-Business Suite Unspecified Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99975, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2019-16278", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Directory Traversal in the function http_verify in nostromo nhttpd through 1.9.6 allows an attacker to achieve remote code execution via a crafted HTTP request.", "cve_id": "CVE-2019-16278", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2019-10-14T17:15:09.427000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94393, "updated_at": "2025-11-06T14:57:37.237000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Directory Traversal in the function http_verify in nostromo nhttpd through 1.9.6 allows an attacker to achieve remote code execution via a crafted HTTP request.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "nhttpd", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2024-11-28", "kev_vuln_name": "Nostromo nhttpd Directory Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99974, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Nostromo"}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-3506", "cvss": 7.4, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0, 12.1.3.0, 12.2.1.0, 12.2.1.1 and 12.2.1.2. Difficult to exploit vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized creation, deletion or modification access to critical data or all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data as well as unauthorized access to critical data or complete access to all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 7.4 (Confidentiality and Integrity impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N).", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-3506", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2017-04-24T19:59:03.037000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.4, "epss_score": 0.94393, "updated_at": "2026-04-22T13:39:47.350000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0, 12.1.3.0, 12.2.1.0, 12.2.1.1 and 12.2.1.2. Difficult to exploit vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized creation, deletion or modification access to critical data or all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data as well as unauthorized access to critical data or complete access to all Oracle WebLogic Server accessible data. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 7.4 (Confidentiality and Integrity impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2024-06-24", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server OS Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99973, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-41773", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "A flaw was found in a change made to path normalization in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.49. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue is known to be exploited in the wild. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and not earlier versions. The fix in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was found to be incomplete, see CVE-2021-42013.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-41773", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-10-05T09:15:07.593000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94391, "updated_at": "2026-02-17T19:49:26.367000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A flaw was found in a change made to path normalization in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.49. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue is known to be exploited in the wild. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and not earlier versions. The fix in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was found to be incomplete, see CVE-2021-42013.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-11-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99973, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-1938", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "When using the Apache JServ Protocol (AJP), care must be taken when trusting incoming connections to Apache Tomcat. Tomcat treats AJP connections as having higher trust than, for example, a similar HTTP connection. If such connections are available to an attacker, they can be exploited in ways that may be surprising. In Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0.30, 8.5.0 to 8.5.50 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.99, Tomcat shipped with an AJP Connector enabled by default that listened on all configured IP addresses. It was expected (and recommended in the security guide) that this Connector would be disabled if not required. This vulnerability report identified a mechanism that allowed: - returning arbitrary files from anywhere in the web application - processing any file in the web application as a JSP Further, if the web application allowed file upload and stored those files within the web application (or the attacker was able to control the content of the web application by some other means) then this, along with the ability to process a file as a JSP, made remote code execution possible. It is important to note that mitigation is only required if an AJP port is accessible to untrusted users. Users wishing to take a defence-in-depth approach and block the vector that permits returning arbitrary files and execution as JSP may upgrade to Apache Tomcat 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later. A number of changes were made to the default AJP Connector configuration in 9.0.31 to harden the default configuration. It is likely that users upgrading to 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later will need to make small changes to their configurations.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-1938", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-02-24T22:15:12.057000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94469, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:37:12.387000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "When using the Apache JServ Protocol (AJP), care must be taken when trusting incoming connections to Apache Tomcat. Tomcat treats AJP connections as having higher trust than, for example, a similar HTTP connection. If such connections are available to an attacker, they can be exploited in ways that may be surprising. In Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0.30, 8.5.0 to 8.5.50 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.99, Tomcat shipped with an AJP Connector enabled by default that listened on all configured IP addresses. It was expected (and recommended in the security guide) that this Connector would be disabled if not required. This vulnerability report identified a mechanism that allowed: - returning arbitrary files from anywhere in the web application - processing any file in the web application as a JSP Further, if the web application allowed file upload and stored those files within the web application (or the attacker was able to control the content of the web application by some other means) then this, along with the ability to process a file as a JSP, made remote code execution possible. It is important to note that mitigation is only required if an AJP port is accessible to untrusted users. Users wishing to take a defence-in-depth approach and block the vector that permits returning arbitrary files and execution as JSP may upgrade to Apache Tomcat 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later. A number of changes were made to the default AJP Connector configuration in 9.0.31 to harden the default configuration. It is likely that users upgrading to 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later will need to make small changes to their configurations.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Tomcat", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-03-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache Tomcat Improper Privilege Management Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99997, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-22963", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "In Spring Cloud Function versions 3.1.6, 3.2.2 and older unsupported versions, when using routing functionality it is possible for a user to provide a specially crafted SpEL as a routing-expression that may result in remote code execution and access to local resources.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-22963", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-04-01T23:15:13.663000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94462, "updated_at": "2025-10-30T19:56:53.730000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "In Spring Cloud Function versions 3.1.6, 3.2.2 and older unsupported versions, when using routing functionality it is possible for a user to provide a specially crafted SpEL as a routing-expression that may result in remote code execution and access to local resources.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Spring Cloud", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-09-15", "kev_vuln_name": "VMware Tanzu Spring Cloud Function Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99995, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "VMware Tanzu"}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-11776", "cvss": 8.1, "desc": "Apache Struts versions 2.3 to 2.3.34 and 2.5 to 2.5.16 suffer from possible Remote Code Execution when alwaysSelectFullNamespace is true (either by user or a plugin like Convention Plugin) and then: results are used with no namespace and in same time, its upper package have no or wildcard namespace and similar to results, same possibility when using url tag which doesn't have value and action set and in same time, its upper package have no or wildcard namespace.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-11776", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2018-08-22T13:29:00.753000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.1, "epss_score": 0.94431, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:38:06.077000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Apache Struts versions 2.3 to 2.3.34 and 2.5 to 2.5.16 suffer from possible Remote Code Execution when alwaysSelectFullNamespace is true (either by user or a plugin like Convention Plugin) and then: results are used with no namespace and in same time, its upper package have no or wildcard namespace and similar to results, same possibility when using url tag which doesn't have value and action set and in same time, its upper package have no or wildcard namespace.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Struts", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache Struts Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99985, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-22965", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "A Spring MVC or Spring WebFlux application running on JDK 9+ may be vulnerable to remote code execution (RCE) via data binding. The specific exploit requires the application to run on Tomcat as a WAR deployment. If the application is deployed as a Spring Boot executable jar, i.e. the default, it is not vulnerable to the exploit. However, the nature of the vulnerability is more general, and there may be other ways to exploit it.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-22965", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-04-01T23:15:13.870000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94428, "updated_at": "2025-10-30T19:56:43.110000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A Spring MVC or Spring WebFlux application running on JDK 9+ may be vulnerable to remote code execution (RCE) via data binding. The specific exploit requires the application to run on Tomcat as a WAR deployment. If the application is deployed as a Spring Boot executable jar, i.e. the default, it is not vulnerable to the exploit. However, the nature of the vulnerability is more general, and there may be other ways to exploit it.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Spring Framework", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-04-25", "kev_vuln_name": "Spring Framework JDK 9+ Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99984, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "VMware"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-17530", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Forced OGNL evaluation, when evaluated on raw user input in tag attributes, may lead to remote code execution. Affected software : Apache Struts 2.0.0 - Struts 2.5.25.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-17530", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-12-11T02:15:10.883000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94376, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:37:20.887000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Forced OGNL evaluation, when evaluated on raw user input in tag attributes, may lead to remote code execution. Affected software : Apache Struts 2.0.0 - Struts 2.5.25.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Struts", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache Struts Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99968, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-12617", "cvss": 8.1, "desc": "When running Apache Tomcat versions 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0, 8.5.0 to 8.5.22, 8.0.0.RC1 to 8.0.46 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.81 with HTTP PUTs enabled (e.g. via setting the readonly initialisation parameter of the Default servlet to false) it was possible to upload a JSP file to the server via a specially crafted request. This JSP could then be requested and any code it contained would be executed by the server.", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-12617", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2017-10-04T01:29:02.120000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.1, "epss_score": 0.94356, "updated_at": "2026-04-21T17:03:52.243000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "When running Apache Tomcat versions 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0, 8.5.0 to 8.5.22, 8.0.0.RC1 to 8.0.46 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.81 with HTTP PUTs enabled (e.g. via setting the readonly initialisation parameter of the Default servlet to false) it was possible to upload a JSP file to the server via a specially crafted request. This JSP could then be requested and any code it contained would be executed by the server.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Tomcat", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-04-15", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache Tomcat Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99962, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2023-34362", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "In Progress MOVEit Transfer before 2021.0.6 (13.0.6), 2021.1.4 (13.1.4), 2022.0.4 (14.0.4), 2022.1.5 (14.1.5), and 2023.0.1 (15.0.1), a SQL injection vulnerability has been found in the MOVEit Transfer web application that could allow an unauthenticated attacker to gain access to MOVEit Transfer's database. Depending on the database engine being used (MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server, or Azure SQL), an attacker may be able to infer information about the structure and contents of the database, and execute SQL statements that alter or delete database elements. NOTE: this is exploited in the wild in May and June 2023; exploitation of unpatched systems can occur via HTTP or HTTPS. All versions (e.g., 2020.0 and 2019x) before the five explicitly mentioned versions are affected, including older unsupported versions.", "cve_id": "CVE-2023-34362", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2023-06-02T14:15:09.487000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94254, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T14:37:08.460000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "In Progress MOVEit Transfer before 2021.0.6 (13.0.6), 2021.1.4 (13.1.4), 2022.0.4 (14.0.4), 2022.1.5 (14.1.5), and 2023.0.1 (15.0.1), a SQL injection vulnerability has been found in the MOVEit Transfer web application that could allow an unauthenticated attacker to gain access to MOVEit Transfer's database. Depending on the database engine being used (MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server, or Azure SQL), an attacker may be able to infer information about the structure and contents of the database, and execute SQL statements that alter or delete database elements. NOTE: this is exploited in the wild in May and June 2023; exploitation of unpatched systems can occur via HTTP or HTTPS. All versions (e.g., 2020.0 and 2019x) before the five explicitly mentioned versions are affected, including older unsupported versions.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "MOVEit Transfer", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-06-23", "kev_vuln_name": "Progress MOVEit Transfer SQL Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99934, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Progress"}, {"cve": "CVE-2016-8735", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Remote code execution is possible with Apache Tomcat before 6.0.48, 7.x before 7.0.73, 8.x before 8.0.39, 8.5.x before 8.5.7, and 9.x before 9.0.0.M12 if JmxRemoteLifecycleListener is used and an attacker can reach JMX ports. The issue exists because this listener wasn't updated for consistency with the CVE-2016-3427 Oracle patch that affected credential types.", "cve_id": "CVE-2016-8735", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2017-04-06T21:59:00.243000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.93871, "updated_at": "2026-04-21T17:03:44.873000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Remote code execution is possible with Apache Tomcat before 6.0.48, 7.x before 7.0.73, 8.x before 8.0.39, 8.5.x before 8.5.7, and 9.x before 9.0.0.M12 if JmxRemoteLifecycleListener is used and an attacker can reach JMX ports. The issue exists because this listener wasn't updated for consistency with the CVE-2016-3427 Oracle patch that affected credential types.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Tomcat", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-06-02", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache Tomcat Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99872, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2012-2122", "cvss": 5.1, "desc": "sql/password.c in Oracle MySQL 5.1.x before 5.1.63, 5.5.x before 5.5.24, and 5.6.x before 5.6.6, and MariaDB 5.1.x before 5.1.62, 5.2.x before 5.2.12, 5.3.x before 5.3.6, and 5.5.x before 5.5.23, when running in certain environments with certain implementations of the memcmp function, allows remote attackers to bypass authentication by repeatedly authenticating with the same incorrect password, which eventually causes a token comparison to succeed due to an improperly-checked return value.", "cve_id": "CVE-2012-2122", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2012-06-26T18:55:05.083000+05:30", "cvss_score": 5.1, "epss_score": 0.94058, "updated_at": "2025-04-11T00:51:21.963000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:H/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P", "description": "sql/password.c in Oracle MySQL 5.1.x before 5.1.63, 5.5.x before 5.5.24, and 5.6.x before 5.6.6, and MariaDB 5.1.x before 5.1.62, 5.2.x before 5.2.12, 5.3.x before 5.3.6, and 5.5.x before 5.5.23, when running in certain environments with certain implementations of the memcmp function, allows remote attackers to bypass authentication by repeatedly authenticating with the same incorrect password, which eventually causes a token comparison to succeed due to an improperly-checked return value.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 58.02, "epss_percentile": 0.99904, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-5645", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "In Apache Log4j 2.x before 2.8.2, when using the TCP socket server or UDP socket server to receive serialized log events from another application, a specially crafted binary payload can be sent that, when deserialized, can execute arbitrary code.", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-5645", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2017-04-17T21:59:00.373000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94013, "updated_at": "2025-04-20T01:37:25.860000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "In Apache Log4j 2.x before 2.8.2, when using the TCP socket server or UDP socket server to receive serialized log events from another application, a specially crafted binary payload can be sent that, when deserialized, can execute arbitrary code.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 76.81, "epss_percentile": 0.99898, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2019-0230", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Apache Struts 2.0.0 to 2.5.20 forced double OGNL evaluation, when evaluated on raw user input in tag attributes, may lead to remote code execution.", "cve_id": "CVE-2019-0230", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-09-14T17:15:09.933000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.93849, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T04:16:32.927000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Apache Struts 2.0.0 to 2.5.20 forced double OGNL evaluation, when evaluated on raw user input in tag attributes, may lead to remote code execution.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 76.74, "epss_percentile": 0.99868, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-9484", "cvss": 7.0, "desc": "When using Apache Tomcat versions 10.0.0-M1 to 10.0.0-M4, 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.34, 8.5.0 to 8.5.54 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.103 if a) an attacker is able to control the contents and name of a file on the server; and b) the server is configured to use the PersistenceManager with a FileStore; and c) the PersistenceManager is configured with sessionAttributeValueClassNameFilter=\\"null\\" (the default unless a SecurityManager is used) or a sufficiently lax filter to allow the attacker provided object to be deserialized; and d) the attacker knows the relative file path from the storage location used by FileStore to the file the attacker has control over; then, using a specifically crafted request, the attacker will be able to trigger remote code execution via deserialization of the file under their control. Note that all of conditions a) to d) must be true for the attack to succeed.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-9484", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-05-20T19:15:09.257000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.0, "epss_score": 0.93464, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T05:40:44.420000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "When using Apache Tomcat versions 10.0.0-M1 to 10.0.0-M4, 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.34, 8.5.0 to 8.5.54 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.103 if a) an attacker is able to control the contents and name of a file on the server; and b) the server is configured to use the PersistenceManager with a FileStore; and c) the PersistenceManager is configured with sessionAttributeValueClassNameFilter=\\"null\\" (the default unless a SecurityManager is used) or a sufficiently lax filter to allow the attacker provided object to be deserialized; and d) the attacker knows the relative file path from the storage location used by FileStore to the file the attacker has control over; then, using a specifically crafted request, the attacker will be able to trigger remote code execution via deserialization of the file under their control. Note that all of conditions a) to d) must be true for the attack to succeed.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 65.39, "epss_percentile": 0.99827, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-29442", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "Nacos is a platform designed for dynamic service discovery and configuration and service management. In Nacos before version 1.4.1, the ConfigOpsController lets the user perform management operations like querying the database or even wiping it out. While the /data/remove endpoint is properly protected with the @Secured annotation, the /derby endpoint is not protected and can be openly accessed by unauthenticated users. These endpoints are only valid when using embedded storage (derby DB) so this issue should not affect those installations using external storage (e.g. mysql)", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-29442", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2021-04-27T21:15:08.030000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.92758, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T06:01:06.423000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "description": "Nacos is a platform designed for dynamic service discovery and configuration and service management. In Nacos before version 1.4.1, the ConfigOpsController lets the user perform management operations like querying the database or even wiping it out. While the /data/remove endpoint is properly protected with the @Secured annotation, the /derby endpoint is not protected and can be openly accessed by unauthenticated users. These endpoints are only valid when using embedded storage (derby DB) so this issue should not affect those installations using external storage (e.g. mysql)", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 67.1, "epss_percentile": 0.99763, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2008-0226", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "Multiple buffer overflows in yaSSL 1.7.5 and earlier, as used in MySQL and possibly other products, allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via (1) the ProcessOldClientHello function in handshake.cpp or (2) \\"input_buffer& operator>>\\" in yassl_imp.cpp.", "cve_id": "CVE-2008-0226", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2008-01-10T23:46:00+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.92203, "updated_at": "2026-04-23T00:35:47.467000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P", "description": "Multiple buffer overflows in yaSSL 1.7.5 and earlier, as used in MySQL and possibly other products, allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via (1) the ProcessOldClientHello function in handshake.cpp or (2) \\"input_buffer& operator>>\\" in yassl_imp.cpp.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 66.88, "epss_percentile": 0.99721, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-21351", "cvss": 9.1, "desc": "XStream is a Java library to serialize objects to XML and back again. In XStream before version 1.4.16, there is a vulnerability may allow a remote attacker to load and execute arbitrary code from a remote host only by manipulating the processed input stream. No user is affected, who followed the recommendation to setup XStream's security framework with a whitelist limited to the minimal required types. If you rely on XStream's default blacklist of the Security Framework, you will have to use at least version 1.4.16.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-21351", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-03-23T00:15:13.367000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.1, "epss_score": 0.92, "updated_at": "2025-05-23T17:34:20.440000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "XStream is a Java library to serialize objects to XML and back again. In XStream before version 1.4.16, there is a vulnerability may allow a remote attacker to load and execute arbitrary code from a remote host only by manipulating the processed input stream. No user is affected, who followed the recommendation to setup XStream's security framework with a whitelist limited to the minimal required types. If you rely on XStream's default blacklist of the Security Framework, you will have to use at least version 1.4.16.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 73.2, "epss_percentile": 0.99706, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-13935", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "The payload length in a WebSocket frame was not correctly validated in Apache Tomcat 10.0.0-M1 to 10.0.0-M6, 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.36, 8.5.0 to 8.5.56 and 7.0.27 to 7.0.104. Invalid payload lengths could trigger an infinite loop. Multiple requests with invalid payload lengths could lead to a denial of service.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-13935", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-07-14T15:15:11.070000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.91745, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T05:02:10.907000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "The payload length in a WebSocket frame was not correctly validated in Apache Tomcat 10.0.0-M1 to 10.0.0-M6, 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.36, 8.5.0 to 8.5.56 and 7.0.27 to 7.0.104. Invalid payload lengths could trigger an infinite loop. Multiple requests with invalid payload lengths could lead to a denial of service.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 66.7, "epss_percentile": 0.9969, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-5777", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "MAGMI versions prior to 0.7.24 are vulnerable to a remote authentication bypass due to allowing default credentials in the event there is a database connection failure. A remote attacker can trigger this connection failure if the Mysql setting max_connections (default 151) is lower than Apache (or another web server) setting MaxRequestWorkers (formerly MaxClients) (default 256). This can be done by sending at least 151 simultaneous requests to the Magento website to trigger a \\"Too many connections\\" error, then use default magmi:magmi basic authentication to remotely bypass authentication.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-5777", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-09-01T21:15:12.660000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.91472, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T05:34:34.950000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "MAGMI versions prior to 0.7.24 are vulnerable to a remote authentication bypass due to allowing default credentials in the event there is a database connection failure. A remote attacker can trigger this connection failure if the Mysql setting max_connections (default 151) is lower than Apache (or another web server) setting MaxRequestWorkers (formerly MaxClients) (default 256). This can be done by sending at least 151 simultaneous requests to the Magento website to trigger a \\"Too many connections\\" error, then use default magmi:magmi basic authentication to remotely bypass authentication.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 75.79, "epss_percentile": 0.99674, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-7251", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An issue was discovered in config/error.php in Anchor 0.12.3. The error log is exposed at an errors.log URI, and contains MySQL credentials if a MySQL error (such as \\"Too many connections\\") has occurred.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-7251", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2018-02-19T22:29:00.220000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.90603, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T04:11:53.003000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An issue was discovered in config/error.php in Anchor 0.12.3. The error log is exposed at an errors.log URI, and contains MySQL credentials if a MySQL error (such as \\"Too many connections\\") has occurred.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 75.44, "epss_percentile": 0.99622, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2014-2323", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "SQL injection vulnerability in mod_mysql_vhost.c in lighttpd before 1.4.35 allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary SQL commands via the host name, related to request_check_hostname.", "cve_id": "CVE-2014-2323", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2014-03-14T15:55:05.743000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.90366, "updated_at": "2025-04-12T10:46:40.837000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "SQL injection vulnerability in mod_mysql_vhost.c in lighttpd before 1.4.35 allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary SQL commands via the host name, related to request_check_hostname.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 75.35, "epss_percentile": 0.99607, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-5398", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "In Spring Framework, versions 5.2.x prior to 5.2.3, versions 5.1.x prior to 5.1.13, and versions 5.0.x prior to 5.0.16, an application is vulnerable to a reflected file download (RFD) attack when it sets a \\"Content-Disposition\\" header in the response where the filename attribute is derived from user supplied input.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-5398", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-01-17T00:15:12.103000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.90184, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T05:34:04.053000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "In Spring Framework, versions 5.2.x prior to 5.2.3, versions 5.1.x prior to 5.1.13, and versions 5.0.x prior to 5.0.16, an application is vulnerable to a reflected file download (RFD) attack when it sets a \\"Content-Disposition\\" header in the response where the filename attribute is derived from user supplied input.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 66.07, "epss_percentile": 0.99594, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2019-9193", "cvss": 7.2, "desc": "In PostgreSQL 9.3 through 11.2, the \\"COPY TO/FROM PROGRAM\\" function allows superusers and users in the 'pg_execute_server_program' group to execute arbitrary code in the context of the database's operating system user. This functionality is enabled by default and can be abused to run arbitrary operating system commands on Windows, Linux, and macOS. NOTE: Third parties claim/state this is not an issue because PostgreSQL functionality for ‘COPY TO/FROM PROGRAM’ is acting as intended. References state that in PostgreSQL, a superuser can execute commands as the server user without using the ‘COPY FROM PROGRAM’.", "cve_id": "CVE-2019-9193", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2019-04-01T21:30:45.110000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.2, "epss_score": 0.93401, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T04:51:10.670000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "In PostgreSQL 9.3 through 11.2, the \\"COPY TO/FROM PROGRAM\\" function allows superusers and users in the 'pg_execute_server_program' group to execute arbitrary code in the context of the database's operating system user. This functionality is enabled by default and can be abused to run arbitrary operating system commands on Windows, Linux, and macOS. NOTE: Third parties claim/state this is not an issue because PostgreSQL functionality for ‘COPY TO/FROM PROGRAM’ is acting as intended. References state that in PostgreSQL, a superuser can execute commands as the server user without using the ‘COPY FROM PROGRAM’.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 66.16, "epss_percentile": 0.99821, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-4223", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "The pgAdmin server includes an HTTP API that is intended to be used to validate the path a user selects to external PostgreSQL utilities such as pg_dump and pg_restore. The utility is executed by the server to determine what PostgreSQL version it is from. Versions of pgAdmin prior to 6.17 failed to properly secure this API, which could allow an unauthenticated user to call it with a path of their choosing, such as a UNC path to a server they control on a Windows machine. This would cause an appropriately named executable in the target path to be executed by the pgAdmin server.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-4223", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2022-12-13T16:15:26.277000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.87793, "updated_at": "2025-04-14T19:15:34.730000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "The pgAdmin server includes an HTTP API that is intended to be used to validate the path a user selects to external PostgreSQL utilities such as pg_dump and pg_restore. The utility is executed by the server to determine what PostgreSQL version it is from. Versions of pgAdmin prior to 6.17 failed to properly secure this API, which could allow an unauthenticated user to call it with a path of their choosing, such as a UNC path to a server they control on a Windows machine. This would cause an appropriately named executable in the target path to be executed by the pgAdmin server.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 70.32, "epss_percentile": 0.99478, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-44427", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An unauthenticated SQL Injection vulnerability in Rosario Student Information System (aka rosariosis) before 8.1.1 allows remote attackers to execute PostgreSQL statements (e.g., SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE) through /Side.php via the syear parameter.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-44427", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-11-29T22:15:07.533000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.83869, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T06:30:57.080000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An unauthenticated SQL Injection vulnerability in Rosario Student Information System (aka rosariosis) before 8.1.1 allows remote attackers to execute PostgreSQL statements (e.g., SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE) through /Side.php via the syear parameter.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 72.75, "epss_percentile": 0.99302, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2025-1094", "cvss": 8.1, "desc": "Improper neutralization of quoting syntax in PostgreSQL libpq functions PQescapeLiteral(), PQescapeIdentifier(), PQescapeString(), and PQescapeStringConn() allows a database input provider to achieve SQL injection in certain usage patterns.  Specifically, SQL injection requires the application to use the function result to construct input to psql, the PostgreSQL interactive terminal.  Similarly, improper neutralization of quoting syntax in PostgreSQL command line utility programs allows a source of command line arguments to achieve SQL injection when client_encoding is BIG5 and server_encoding is one of EUC_TW or MULE_INTERNAL.  Versions before PostgreSQL 17.3, 16.7, 15.11, 14.16, and 13.19 are affected.", "cve_id": "CVE-2025-1094", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2025-02-13T13:15:09.130000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.1, "epss_score": 0.83359, "updated_at": "2026-04-15T00:35:42.020000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Improper neutralization of quoting syntax in PostgreSQL libpq functions PQescapeLiteral(), PQescapeIdentifier(), PQescapeString(), and PQescapeStringConn() allows a database input provider to achieve SQL injection in certain usage patterns.  Specifically, SQL injection requires the application to use the function result to construct input to psql, the PostgreSQL interactive terminal.  Similarly, improper neutralization of quoting syntax in PostgreSQL command line utility programs allows a source of command line arguments to achieve SQL injection when client_encoding is BIG5 and server_encoding is one of EUC_TW or MULE_INTERNAL.  Versions before PostgreSQL 17.3, 16.7, 15.11, 14.16, and 13.19 are affected.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 65.74, "epss_percentile": 0.99278, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-1058", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "A flaw was found in the way Postgresql allowed a user to modify the behavior of a query for other users. An attacker with a user account could use this flaw to execute code with the permissions of superuser in the database. Versions 9.3 through 10 are affected.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-1058", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2018-03-02T15:29:00.337000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.82687, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T03:59:05.280000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A flaw was found in the way Postgresql allowed a user to modify the behavior of a query for other users. An attacker with a user account could use this flaw to execute code with the permissions of superuser in the database. Versions 9.3 through 10 are affected.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 68.27, "epss_percentile": 0.99247, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2013-1899", "cvss": 6.5, "desc": "Argument injection vulnerability in PostgreSQL 9.2.x before 9.2.4, 9.1.x before 9.1.9, and 9.0.x before 9.0.13 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (file corruption), and allows remote authenticated users to modify configuration settings and execute arbitrary code, via a connection request using a database name that begins with a \\"-\\" (hyphen).", "cve_id": "CVE-2013-1899", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2013-04-04T17:55:00.877000+05:30", "cvss_score": 6.5, "epss_score": 0.81124, "updated_at": "2025-04-11T00:51:21.963000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:S/C:P/I:P/A:P", "description": "Argument injection vulnerability in PostgreSQL 9.2.x before 9.2.4, 9.1.x before 9.1.9, and 9.0.x before 9.0.13 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (file corruption), and allows remote authenticated users to modify configuration settings and execute arbitrary code, via a connection request using a database name that begins with a \\"-\\" (hyphen).", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P1", "priority_score": 58.45, "epss_percentile": 0.99165, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2024-55964", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An issue was discovered in Appsmith before 1.52. An incorrectly configured PostgreSQL instance in the Appsmith image leads to remote command execution inside the Appsmith Docker container. The attacker must be able to access Appsmith, login to it, create a datasource, create a query against that datasource, and execute that query.", "cve_id": "CVE-2024-55964", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2025-03-26T20:15:21.373000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.67337, "updated_at": "2025-04-01T16:34:34.710000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An issue was discovered in Appsmith before 1.52. An incorrectly configured PostgreSQL instance in the Appsmith image leads to remote command execution inside the Appsmith Docker container. The attacker must be able to access Appsmith, login to it, create a datasource, create a query against that datasource, and execute that query.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P2", "priority_score": 66.13, "epss_percentile": 0.98576, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2024-39887", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An SQL Injection vulnerability in Apache Superset exists due to improper neutralization of special elements used in SQL commands. Specifically, certain engine-specific functions are not checked, which allows attackers to bypass Apache Superset's SQL authorization. To mitigate this, a new configuration key named DISALLOWED_SQL_FUNCTIONS has been introduced. This key disallows the use of the following PostgreSQL functions: version, query_to_xml, inet_server_addr, and inet_client_addr. Additional functions can be added to this list for increased protection.\\n\\nThis issue affects Apache Superset: before 4.0.2.\\n\\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 4.0.2, which fixes the issue.", "cve_id": "CVE-2024-39887", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2024-07-16T10:15:03.380000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.63842, "updated_at": "2025-02-13T18:18:09.337000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An SQL Injection vulnerability in Apache Superset exists due to improper neutralization of special elements used in SQL commands. Specifically, certain engine-specific functions are not checked, which allows attackers to bypass Apache Superset's SQL authorization. To mitigate this, a new configuration key named DISALLOWED_SQL_FUNCTIONS has been introduced. This key disallows the use of the following PostgreSQL functions: version, query_to_xml, inet_server_addr, and inet_client_addr. Additional functions can be added to this list for increased protection.\\n\\nThis issue affects Apache Superset: before 4.0.2.\\n\\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 4.0.2, which fixes the issue.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P2", "priority_score": 64.74, "epss_percentile": 0.98436, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2005-3656", "cvss": 10.0, "desc": "Multiple format string vulnerabilities in logging functions in mod_auth_pgsql before 2.0.3, when used for user authentication against a PostgreSQL database, allows remote unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code, as demonstrated via the username.", "cve_id": "CVE-2005-3656", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2005-12-31T05:00:00+05:30", "cvss_score": 10.0, "epss_score": 0.49577, "updated_at": "2026-04-16T00:27:16.627000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:C/I:C/A:C", "description": "Multiple format string vulnerabilities in logging functions in mod_auth_pgsql before 2.0.3, when used for user authentication against a PostgreSQL database, allows remote unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code, as demonstrated via the username.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P2", "priority_score": 59.83, "epss_percentile": 0.97812, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2007-3280", "cvss": 9.0, "desc": "The Database Link library (dblink) in PostgreSQL 8.1 implements functions via CREATE statements that map to arbitrary libraries based on the C programming language, which allows remote authenticated superusers to map and execute a function from any library, as demonstrated by using the system function in libc.so.6 to gain shell access.", "cve_id": "CVE-2007-3280", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2007-06-19T21:30:00+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.0, "epss_score": 0.48919, "updated_at": "2026-04-23T00:35:47.467000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:S/C:C/I:C/A:C", "description": "The Database Link library (dblink) in PostgreSQL 8.1 implements functions via CREATE statements that map to arbitrary libraries based on the C programming language, which allows remote authenticated superusers to map and execute a function from any library, as demonstrated by using the system function in libc.so.6 to gain shell access.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P2", "priority_score": 55.57, "epss_percentile": 0.97778, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-7546", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "PostgreSQL versions before 9.2.22, 9.3.18, 9.4.13, 9.5.8 and 9.6.4 are vulnerable to incorrect authentication flaw allowing remote attackers to gain access to database accounts with an empty password.", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-7546", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2017-08-16T18:29:00.207000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.33122, "updated_at": "2025-04-20T01:37:25.860000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "PostgreSQL versions before 9.2.22, 9.3.18, 9.4.13, 9.5.8 and 9.6.4 are vulnerable to incorrect authentication flaw allowing remote attackers to gain access to database accounts with an empty password.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P2", "priority_score": 52.45, "epss_percentile": 0.96921, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2015-1352", "cvss": 5.0, "desc": "The build_tablename function in pgsql.c in the PostgreSQL (aka pgsql) extension in PHP through 5.6.7 does not validate token extraction for table names, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (NULL pointer dereference and application crash) via a crafted name.", "cve_id": "CVE-2015-1352", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2015-03-30T10:59:08.770000+05:30", "cvss_score": 5.0, "epss_score": 0.30855, "updated_at": "2025-04-12T10:46:40.837000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:N/I:N/A:P", "description": "The build_tablename function in pgsql.c in the PostgreSQL (aka pgsql) extension in PHP through 5.6.7 does not validate token extraction for table names, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (NULL pointer dereference and application crash) via a crafted name.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 32.34, "epss_percentile": 0.96747, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2023-5002", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "A flaw was found in pgAdmin. This issue occurs when the pgAdmin server HTTP API validates the path a user selects to external PostgreSQL utilities such as pg_dump and pg_restore. Versions of pgAdmin prior to 7.6 failed to properly control the server code executed on this API, allowing an authenticated user to run arbitrary commands on the server.", "cve_id": "CVE-2023-5002", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2023-09-22T14:15:47.213000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.27209, "updated_at": "2025-03-17T16:43:52.873000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A flaw was found in pgAdmin. This issue occurs when the pgAdmin server HTTP API validates the path a user selects to external PostgreSQL utilities such as pg_dump and pg_restore. Versions of pgAdmin prior to 7.6 failed to properly control the server code executed on this API, allowing an authenticated user to run arbitrary commands on the server.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 46.08, "epss_percentile": 0.96406, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-15099", "cvss": 6.5, "desc": "INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE commands in PostgreSQL 10.x before 10.1, 9.6.x before 9.6.6, and 9.5.x before 9.5.10 disclose table contents that the invoker lacks privilege to read. These exploits affect only tables where the attacker lacks full read access but has both INSERT and UPDATE privileges. Exploits bypass row level security policies and lack of SELECT privilege.", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-15099", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2017-11-22T18:29:00.583000+05:30", "cvss_score": 6.5, "epss_score": 0.27111, "updated_at": "2025-04-20T01:37:25.860000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "description": "INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE commands in PostgreSQL 10.x before 10.1, 9.6.x before 9.6.6, and 9.5.x before 9.5.10 disclose table contents that the invoker lacks privilege to read. These exploits affect only tables where the attacker lacks full read access but has both INSERT and UPDATE privileges. Exploits bypass row level security policies and lack of SELECT privilege.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P4", "priority_score": 36.84, "epss_percentile": 0.96396, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2014-6395", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "Heap-based buffer overflow in the dissector_postgresql function in dissectors/ec_postgresql.c in Ettercap before 0.8.1 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service or possibly execute arbitrary code via a crafted password length value that is inconsistent with the actual length of the password.", "cve_id": "CVE-2014-6395", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2014-12-19T15:59:06.033000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.26583, "updated_at": "2025-04-12T10:46:40.837000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P", "description": "Heap-based buffer overflow in the dissector_postgresql function in dissectors/ec_postgresql.c in Ettercap before 0.8.1 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service or possibly execute arbitrary code via a crafted password length value that is inconsistent with the actual length of the password.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 40.63, "epss_percentile": 0.96351, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-25695", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "A flaw was found in PostgreSQL versions before 13.1, before 12.5, before 11.10, before 10.15, before 9.6.20 and before 9.5.24. An attacker having permission to create non-temporary objects in at least one schema can execute arbitrary SQL functions under the identity of a superuser. The highest threat from this vulnerability is to data confidentiality and integrity as well as system availability.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-25695", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-11-16T01:15:12.780000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.23757, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T05:18:29.807000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A flaw was found in PostgreSQL versions before 13.1, before 12.5, before 11.10, before 10.15, before 9.6.20 and before 9.5.24. An attacker having permission to create non-temporary objects in at least one schema can execute arbitrary SQL functions under the identity of a superuser. The highest threat from this vulnerability is to data confidentiality and integrity as well as system availability.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 44.7, "epss_percentile": 0.96023, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2005-0245", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "Buffer overflow in gram.y for PostgreSQL 8.0.0 and earlier may allow attackers to execute arbitrary code via a large number of arguments to a refcursor function (gram.y), which leads to a heap-based buffer overflow, a different vulnerability than CVE-2005-0247.", "cve_id": "CVE-2005-0245", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2005-02-01T05:00:00+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.23114, "updated_at": "2026-04-16T00:27:16.627000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:P", "description": "Buffer overflow in gram.y for PostgreSQL 8.0.0 and earlier may allow attackers to execute arbitrary code via a large number of arguments to a refcursor function (gram.y), which leads to a heap-based buffer overflow, a different vulnerability than CVE-2005-0247.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 39.25, "epss_percentile": 0.95947, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2010-0442", "cvss": 6.5, "desc": "The bitsubstr function in backend/utils/adt/varbit.c in PostgreSQL 8.0.23, 8.1.11, and 8.3.8 allows remote authenticated users to cause a denial of service (daemon crash) or have unspecified other impact via vectors involving a negative integer in the third argument, as demonstrated by a SELECT statement that contains a call to the substring function for a bit string, related to an \\"overflow.\\"", "cve_id": "CVE-2010-0442", "in_kev": false, "severity": "Medium", "published": "2010-02-02T18:30:00.360000+05:30", "cvss_score": 6.5, "epss_score": 0.13526, "updated_at": "2025-04-11T00:51:21.963000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "AV:N/AC:L/Au:S/C:P/I:P/A:P", "description": "The bitsubstr function in backend/utils/adt/varbit.c in PostgreSQL 8.0.23, 8.1.11, and 8.3.8 allows remote authenticated users to cause a denial of service (daemon crash) or have unspecified other impact via vectors involving a negative integer in the third argument, as demonstrated by a SELECT statement that contains a call to the substring function for a bit string, related to an \\"overflow.\\"", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "2.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P4", "priority_score": 31.41, "epss_percentile": 0.94243, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2019-10164", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "PostgreSQL versions 10.x before 10.9 and versions 11.x before 11.4 are vulnerable to a stack-based buffer overflow. Any authenticated user can overflow a stack-based buffer by changing the user's own password to a purpose-crafted value. This often suffices to execute arbitrary code as the PostgreSQL operating system account.", "cve_id": "CVE-2019-10164", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2019-06-26T16:15:09.707000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.13393, "updated_at": "2024-11-21T04:18:33.377000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "PostgreSQL versions 10.x before 10.9 and versions 11.x before 11.4 are vulnerable to a stack-based buffer overflow. Any authenticated user can overflow a stack-based buffer by changing the user's own password to a purpose-crafted value. This often suffices to execute arbitrary code as the PostgreSQL operating system account.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 40.56, "epss_percentile": 0.94213, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2016-0773", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "PostgreSQL before 9.1.20, 9.2.x before 9.2.15, 9.3.x before 9.3.11, 9.4.x before 9.4.6, and 9.5.x before 9.5.1 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (infinite loop or buffer overflow and crash) via a large Unicode character range in a regular expression.", "cve_id": "CVE-2016-0773", "in_kev": false, "severity": "High", "published": "2016-02-17T15:59:02.687000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.12452, "updated_at": "2025-04-12T10:46:40.837000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "PostgreSQL before 9.1.20, 9.2.x before 9.2.15, 9.3.x before 9.3.11, 9.4.x before 9.4.6, and 9.5.x before 9.5.1 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (infinite loop or buffer overflow and crash) via a large Unicode character range in a regular expression.", "has_exploit": false, "kev_product": null, "cvss_version": "3.0", "kev_due_date": null, "kev_vuln_name": null, "priority_level": "P3", "priority_score": 34.98, "epss_percentile": 0.93933, "exploit_sources": [], "kev_vendor_project": null}, {"cve": "CVE-2017-1000353", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Jenkins versions 2.56 and earlier as well as 2.46.1 LTS and earlier are vulnerable to an unauthenticated remote code execution. An unauthenticated remote code execution vulnerability allowed attackers to transfer a serialized Java `SignedObject` object to the Jenkins CLI, that would be deserialized using a new `ObjectInputStream`, bypassing the existing blacklist-based protection mechanism. We're fixing this issue by adding `SignedObject` to the blacklist. We're also backporting the new HTTP CLI protocol from Jenkins 2.54 to LTS 2.46.2, and deprecating the remoting-based (i.e. Java serialization) CLI protocol, disabling it by default.", "cve_id": "CVE-2017-1000353", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2018-01-29T17:29:00.193000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94482, "updated_at": "2025-11-05T19:24:40.943000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Jenkins versions 2.56 and earlier as well as 2.46.1 LTS and earlier are vulnerable to an unauthenticated remote code execution. An unauthenticated remote code execution vulnerability allowed attackers to transfer a serialized Java `SignedObject` object to the Jenkins CLI, that would be deserialized using a new `ObjectInputStream`, bypassing the existing blacklist-based protection mechanism. We're fixing this issue by adding `SignedObject` to the blacklist. We're also backporting the new HTTP CLI protocol from Jenkins 2.54 to LTS 2.46.2, and deprecating the remoting-based (i.e. Java serialization) CLI protocol, disabling it by default.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Jenkins", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2025-10-23", "kev_vuln_name": "Jenkins Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99999, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Jenkins"}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-13379", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory (\\"Path Traversal\\") in Fortinet FortiOS 6.0.0 to 6.0.4, 5.6.3 to 5.6.7 and 5.4.6 to 5.4.12 and FortiProxy 2.0.0, 1.2.0 to 1.2.8, 1.1.0 to 1.1.6, 1.0.0 to 1.0.7 under SSL VPN web portal allows an unauthenticated attacker to download system files via special crafted HTTP resource requests.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-13379", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2019-06-04T21:29:00.233000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94473, "updated_at": "2025-10-24T12:53:03.100000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory (\\"Path Traversal\\") in Fortinet FortiOS 6.0.0 to 6.0.4, 5.6.3 to 5.6.7 and 5.4.6 to 5.4.12 and FortiProxy 2.0.0, 1.2.0 to 1.2.8, 1.1.0 to 1.1.6, 1.0.0 to 1.0.7 under SSL VPN web portal allows an unauthenticated attacker to download system files via special crafted HTTP resource requests.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "FortiOS", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Fortinet FortiOS SSL VPN Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99999, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Fortinet"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-46169", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Cacti is an open source platform which provides a robust and extensible operational monitoring and fault management framework for users. In affected versions a command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary code on a server running Cacti, if a specific data source was selected for any monitored device. The vulnerability resides in the `remote_agent.php` file. This file can be accessed without authentication. This function retrieves the IP address of the client via `get_client_addr` and resolves this IP address to the corresponding hostname via `gethostbyaddr`. After this, it is verified that an entry within the `poller` table exists, where the hostname corresponds to the resolved hostname. If such an entry was found, the function returns `true` and the client is authorized. This authorization can be bypassed due to the implementation of the `get_client_addr` function. The function is defined in the file `lib/functions.php` and checks serval `$_SERVER` variables to determine the IP address of the client. The variables beginning with `HTTP_` can be arbitrarily set by an attacker. Since there is a default entry in the `poller` table with the hostname of the server running Cacti, an attacker can bypass the authentication e.g. by providing the header `Forwarded-For: <TARGETIP>`. This way the function `get_client_addr` returns the IP address of the server running Cacti. The following call to `gethostbyaddr` will resolve this IP address to the hostname of the server, which will pass the `poller` hostname check because of the default entry. After the authorization of the `remote_agent.php` file is bypassed, an attacker can trigger different actions. One of these actions is called `polldata`. The called function `poll_for_data` retrieves a few request parameters and loads the corresponding `poller_item` entries from the database. If the `action` of a `poller_item` equals `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`, the function `proc_open` is used to execute a PHP script. The attacker-controlled parameter `$poller_id` is retrieved via the function `get_nfilter_request_var`, which allows arbitrary strings. This variable is later inserted into the string passed to `proc_open`, which leads to a command injection vulnerability. By e.g. providing the `poller_id=;id` the `id` command is executed. In order to reach the vulnerable call, the attacker must provide a `host_id` and `local_data_id`, where the `action` of the corresponding `poller_item` is set to `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`. Both of these ids (`host_id` and `local_data_id`) can easily be bruteforced. The only requirement is that a `poller_item` with an `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` action exists. This is very likely on a productive instance because this action is added by some predefined templates like `Device - Uptime` or `Device - Polling Time`.\\n\\nThis command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary commands if a `poller_item` with the `action` type `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` (`2`) is configured. The authorization bypass should be prevented by not allowing an attacker to make `get_client_addr` (file `lib/functions.php`) return an arbitrary IP address. This could be done by not honoring the `HTTP_...` `$_SERVER` variables. If these should be kept for compatibility reasons it should at least be prevented to fake the IP address of the server running Cacti. This vulnerability has been addressed in both the 1.2.x and 1.3.x release branches with `1.2.23` being the first release containing the patch.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-46169", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-12-05T21:15:10.527000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94469, "updated_at": "2025-10-24T14:47:01.117000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Cacti is an open source platform which provides a robust and extensible operational monitoring and fault management framework for users. In affected versions a command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary code on a server running Cacti, if a specific data source was selected for any monitored device. The vulnerability resides in the `remote_agent.php` file. This file can be accessed without authentication. This function retrieves the IP address of the client via `get_client_addr` and resolves this IP address to the corresponding hostname via `gethostbyaddr`. After this, it is verified that an entry within the `poller` table exists, where the hostname corresponds to the resolved hostname. If such an entry was found, the function returns `true` and the client is authorized. This authorization can be bypassed due to the implementation of the `get_client_addr` function. The function is defined in the file `lib/functions.php` and checks serval `$_SERVER` variables to determine the IP address of the client. The variables beginning with `HTTP_` can be arbitrarily set by an attacker. Since there is a default entry in the `poller` table with the hostname of the server running Cacti, an attacker can bypass the authentication e.g. by providing the header `Forwarded-For: <TARGETIP>`. This way the function `get_client_addr` returns the IP address of the server running Cacti. The following call to `gethostbyaddr` will resolve this IP address to the hostname of the server, which will pass the `poller` hostname check because of the default entry. After the authorization of the `remote_agent.php` file is bypassed, an attacker can trigger different actions. One of these actions is called `polldata`. The called function `poll_for_data` retrieves a few request parameters and loads the corresponding `poller_item` entries from the database. If the `action` of a `poller_item` equals `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`, the function `proc_open` is used to execute a PHP script. The attacker-controlled parameter `$poller_id` is retrieved via the function `get_nfilter_request_var`, which allows arbitrary strings. This variable is later inserted into the string passed to `proc_open`, which leads to a command injection vulnerability. By e.g. providing the `poller_id=;id` the `id` command is executed. In order to reach the vulnerable call, the attacker must provide a `host_id` and `local_data_id`, where the `action` of the corresponding `poller_item` is set to `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP`. Both of these ids (`host_id` and `local_data_id`) can easily be bruteforced. The only requirement is that a `poller_item` with an `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` action exists. This is very likely on a productive instance because this action is added by some predefined templates like `Device - Uptime` or `Device - Polling Time`.\\n\\nThis command injection vulnerability allows an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary commands if a `poller_item` with the `action` type `POLLER_ACTION_SCRIPT_PHP` (`2`) is configured. The authorization bypass should be prevented by not allowing an attacker to make `get_client_addr` (file `lib/functions.php`) return an arbitrary IP address. This could be done by not honoring the `HTTP_...` `$_SERVER` variables. If these should be kept for compatibility reasons it should at least be prevented to fake the IP address of the server running Cacti. This vulnerability has been addressed in both the 1.2.x and 1.3.x release branches with `1.2.23` being the first release containing the patch.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Cacti", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-03-09", "kev_vuln_name": "Cacti Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99998, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Cacti"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-1938", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "When using the Apache JServ Protocol (AJP), care must be taken when trusting incoming connections to Apache Tomcat. Tomcat treats AJP connections as having higher trust than, for example, a similar HTTP connection. If such connections are available to an attacker, they can be exploited in ways that may be surprising. In Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0.30, 8.5.0 to 8.5.50 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.99, Tomcat shipped with an AJP Connector enabled by default that listened on all configured IP addresses. It was expected (and recommended in the security guide) that this Connector would be disabled if not required. This vulnerability report identified a mechanism that allowed: - returning arbitrary files from anywhere in the web application - processing any file in the web application as a JSP Further, if the web application allowed file upload and stored those files within the web application (or the attacker was able to control the content of the web application by some other means) then this, along with the ability to process a file as a JSP, made remote code execution possible. It is important to note that mitigation is only required if an AJP port is accessible to untrusted users. Users wishing to take a defence-in-depth approach and block the vector that permits returning arbitrary files and execution as JSP may upgrade to Apache Tomcat 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later. A number of changes were made to the default AJP Connector configuration in 9.0.31 to harden the default configuration. It is likely that users upgrading to 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later will need to make small changes to their configurations.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-1938", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-02-24T22:15:12.057000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94469, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:37:12.387000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "When using the Apache JServ Protocol (AJP), care must be taken when trusting incoming connections to Apache Tomcat. Tomcat treats AJP connections as having higher trust than, for example, a similar HTTP connection. If such connections are available to an attacker, they can be exploited in ways that may be surprising. In Apache Tomcat 9.0.0.M1 to 9.0.0.30, 8.5.0 to 8.5.50 and 7.0.0 to 7.0.99, Tomcat shipped with an AJP Connector enabled by default that listened on all configured IP addresses. It was expected (and recommended in the security guide) that this Connector would be disabled if not required. This vulnerability report identified a mechanism that allowed: - returning arbitrary files from anywhere in the web application - processing any file in the web application as a JSP Further, if the web application allowed file upload and stored those files within the web application (or the attacker was able to control the content of the web application by some other means) then this, along with the ability to process a file as a JSP, made remote code execution possible. It is important to note that mitigation is only required if an AJP port is accessible to untrusted users. Users wishing to take a defence-in-depth approach and block the vector that permits returning arbitrary files and execution as JSP may upgrade to Apache Tomcat 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later. A number of changes were made to the default AJP Connector configuration in 9.0.31 to harden the default configuration. It is likely that users upgrading to 9.0.31, 8.5.51 or 7.0.100 or later will need to make small changes to their configurations.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Tomcat", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-03-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache Tomcat Improper Privilege Management Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99997, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2019-2725", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0 and 12.1.3.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2019-2725", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2019-04-26T19:29:00.463000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94468, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:08:18.543000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server component of Oracle Fusion Middleware (subcomponent: Web Services). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0 and 12.1.3.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.0 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-07-10", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server, Injection", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99997, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-14882", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-14882", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-10-21T15:15:25.407000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94454, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:09:11.960000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99992, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-3452", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "A vulnerability in the web services interface of Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to conduct directory traversal attacks and read sensitive files on a targeted system. The vulnerability is due to a lack of proper input validation of URLs in HTTP requests processed by an affected device. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request containing directory traversal character sequences to an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to view arbitrary files within the web services file system on the targeted device. The web services file system is enabled when the affected device is configured with either WebVPN or AnyConnect features. This vulnerability cannot be used to obtain access to ASA or FTD system files or underlying operating system (OS) files.", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-3452", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-07-22T20:15:11.970000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.94452, "updated_at": "2025-10-28T13:54:01.140000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "description": "A vulnerability in the web services interface of Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to conduct directory traversal attacks and read sensitive files on a targeted system. The vulnerability is due to a lack of proper input validation of URLs in HTTP requests processed by an affected device. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request containing directory traversal character sequences to an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to view arbitrary files within the web services file system on the targeted device. The web services file system is enabled when the affected device is configured with either WebVPN or AnyConnect features. This vulnerability cannot be used to obtain access to ASA or FTD system files or underlying operating system (OS) files.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) and Firepower Threat Defense (FTD)", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Cisco ASA and FTD Read-Only Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99992, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Cisco"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-14883", "cvss": 7.2, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows high privileged attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 7.2 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-14883", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2020-10-21T15:15:25.483000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.2, "epss_score": 0.94439, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:09:08.300000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows high privileged attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 7.2 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server Unspecified Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.9999, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2020-14750", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "cve_id": "CVE-2020-14750", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2020-11-02T21:15:24.493000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94438, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:08:31.047000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Vulnerability in the Oracle WebLogic Server product of Oracle Fusion Middleware (component: Console). Supported versions that are affected are 10.3.6.0.0, 12.1.3.0.0, 12.2.1.3.0, 12.2.1.4.0 and 14.1.1.0.0. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via HTTP to compromise Oracle WebLogic Server. Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in takeover of Oracle WebLogic Server. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 9.8 (Confidentiality, Integrity and Availability impacts). CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H).", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "WebLogic Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Oracle WebLogic Server Remote Code Execution Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99988, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Oracle"}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-40438", "cvss": 9.0, "desc": "A crafted request uri-path can cause mod_proxy to forward the request to an origin server choosen by the remote user. This issue affects Apache HTTP Server 2.4.48 and earlier.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-40438", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-09-16T15:15:07.633000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.0, "epss_score": 0.94432, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:37:06.747000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "A crafted request uri-path can cause mod_proxy to forward the request to an origin server choosen by the remote user. This issue affects Apache HTTP Server 2.4.48 and earlier.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Apache", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-12-15", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99986, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-40684", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "An authentication bypass using an alternate path or channel [CWE-288] in Fortinet FortiOS version 7.2.0 through 7.2.1 and 7.0.0 through 7.0.6, FortiProxy version 7.2.0 and version 7.0.0 through 7.0.6 and FortiSwitchManager version 7.2.0 and 7.0.0 allows an unauthenticated atttacker to perform operations on the administrative interface via specially crafted HTTP or HTTPS requests.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-40684", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2022-10-18T14:15:09.747000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94427, "updated_at": "2026-01-14T19:19:58.407000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "An authentication bypass using an alternate path or channel [CWE-288] in Fortinet FortiOS version 7.2.0 through 7.2.1 and 7.0.0 through 7.0.6, FortiProxy version 7.2.0 and version 7.0.0 through 7.0.6 and FortiSwitchManager version 7.2.0 and 7.0.0 allows an unauthenticated atttacker to perform operations on the administrative interface via specially crafted HTTP or HTTPS requests.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Multiple Products", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-11-01", "kev_vuln_name": "Fortinet Multiple Products Authentication Bypass Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99983, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Fortinet"}, {"cve": "CVE-2024-3273", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, was found in D-Link DNS-320L, DNS-325, DNS-327L and DNS-340L up to 20240403. Affected is an unknown function of the file /cgi-bin/nas_sharing.cgi of the component HTTP GET Request Handler. The manipulation of the argument system leads to command injection. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-259284. NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer. NOTE: Vendor was contacted early and confirmed immediately that the product is end-of-life. It should be retired and replaced.", "cve_id": "CVE-2024-3273", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2024-04-04T01:15:50.387000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.94425, "updated_at": "2025-10-30T19:53:04.050000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** A vulnerability, which was classified as critical, was found in D-Link DNS-320L, DNS-325, DNS-327L and DNS-340L up to 20240403. Affected is an unknown function of the file /cgi-bin/nas_sharing.cgi of the component HTTP GET Request Handler. The manipulation of the argument system leads to command injection. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The identifier of this vulnerability is VDB-259284. NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer. NOTE: Vendor was contacted early and confirmed immediately that the product is end-of-life. It should be retired and replaced.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Multiple NAS Devices", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2024-05-02", "kev_vuln_name": "D-Link Multiple NAS Devices Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99982, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "D-Link"}, {"cve": "CVE-2021-42013", "cvss": 9.8, "desc": "It was found that the fix for CVE-2021-41773 in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was insufficient. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and Apache 2.4.50 and not earlier versions.", "cve_id": "CVE-2021-42013", "in_kev": true, "severity": "Critical", "published": "2021-10-07T16:15:09.270000+05:30", "cvss_score": 9.8, "epss_score": 0.9441, "updated_at": "2025-10-27T17:36:49.387000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "It was found that the fix for CVE-2021-41773 in Apache HTTP Server 2.4.50 was insufficient. An attacker could use a path traversal attack to map URLs to files outside the directories configured by Alias-like directives. If files outside of these directories are not protected by the usual default configuration \\"require all denied\\", these requests can succeed. If CGI scripts are also enabled for these aliased pathes, this could allow for remote code execution. This issue only affects Apache 2.4.49 and Apache 2.4.50 and not earlier versions.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP Server", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2021-11-17", "kev_vuln_name": "Apache HTTP Server Path Traversal Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99979, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Apache"}, {"cve": "CVE-2018-0296", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "A vulnerability in the web interface of the Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause an affected device to reload unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition. It is also possible on certain software releases that the ASA will not reload, but an attacker could view sensitive system information without authentication by using directory traversal techniques. The vulnerability is due to lack of proper input validation of the HTTP URL. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request to an affected device. An exploit could allow the attacker to cause a DoS condition or unauthenticated disclosure of information. This vulnerability applies to IPv4 and IPv6 HTTP traffic. This vulnerability affects Cisco ASA Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software that is running on the following Cisco products: 3000 Series Industrial Security Appliance (ISA), ASA 1000V Cloud Firewall, ASA 5500 Series Adaptive Security Appliances, ASA 5500-X Series Next-Generation Firewalls, ASA Services Module for Cisco Catalyst 6500 Series Switches and Cisco 7600 Series Routers, Adaptive Security Virtual Appliance (ASAv), Firepower 2100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 4100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 9300 ASA Security Module, FTD Virtual (FTDv). Cisco Bug IDs: CSCvi16029.", "cve_id": "CVE-2018-0296", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2018-06-07T12:29:00.403000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.94404, "updated_at": "2026-01-14T19:21:29.037000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "A vulnerability in the web interface of the Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause an affected device to reload unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition. It is also possible on certain software releases that the ASA will not reload, but an attacker could view sensitive system information without authentication by using directory traversal techniques. The vulnerability is due to lack of proper input validation of the HTTP URL. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted HTTP request to an affected device. An exploit could allow the attacker to cause a DoS condition or unauthenticated disclosure of information. This vulnerability applies to IPv4 and IPv6 HTTP traffic. This vulnerability affects Cisco ASA Software and Cisco Firepower Threat Defense (FTD) Software that is running on the following Cisco products: 3000 Series Industrial Security Appliance (ISA), ASA 1000V Cloud Firewall, ASA 5500 Series Adaptive Security Appliances, ASA 5500-X Series Next-Generation Firewalls, ASA Services Module for Cisco Catalyst 6500 Series Switches and Cisco 7600 Series Routers, Adaptive Security Virtual Appliance (ASAv), Firepower 2100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 4100 Series Security Appliance, Firepower 9300 ASA Security Module, FTD Virtual (FTDv). Cisco Bug IDs: CSCvi16029.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA)", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-05-03", "kev_vuln_name": "Cisco Adaptive Security Appliance (ASA) Denial-of-Service Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99978, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Cisco"}, {"cve": "CVE-2022-36804", "cvss": 8.8, "desc": "Multiple API endpoints in Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center 7.0.0 before version 7.6.17, from version 7.7.0 before version 7.17.10, from version 7.18.0 before version 7.21.4, from version 8.0.0 before version 8.0.3, from version 8.1.0 before version 8.1.3, and from version 8.2.0 before version 8.2.2, and from version 8.3.0 before 8.3.1 allows remote attackers with read permissions to a public or private Bitbucket repository to execute arbitrary code by sending a malicious HTTP request. This vulnerability was reported via our Bug Bounty Program by TheGrandPew.", "cve_id": "CVE-2022-36804", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2022-08-25T06:15:09.077000+05:30", "cvss_score": 8.8, "epss_score": 0.944, "updated_at": "2025-10-24T13:37:44.367000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "description": "Multiple API endpoints in Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center 7.0.0 before version 7.6.17, from version 7.7.0 before version 7.17.10, from version 7.18.0 before version 7.21.4, from version 8.0.0 before version 8.0.3, from version 8.1.0 before version 8.1.3, and from version 8.2.0 before version 8.2.2, and from version 8.3.0 before 8.3.1 allows remote attackers with read permissions to a public or private Bitbucket repository to execute arbitrary code by sending a malicious HTTP request. This vulnerability was reported via our Bug Bounty Program by TheGrandPew.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "Bitbucket Server and Data Center", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2022-10-21", "kev_vuln_name": "Atlassian Bitbucket Server and Data Center Command Injection Vulnerability", "priority_level": "P0", "priority_score": 100.0, "epss_percentile": 0.99977, "exploit_sources": ["CISA KEV"], "kev_vendor_project": "Atlassian"}, {"cve": "CVE-2023-44487", "cvss": 7.5, "desc": "The HTTP/2 protocol allows a denial of service (server resource consumption) because request cancellation can reset many streams quickly, as exploited in the wild in August through October 2023.", "cve_id": "CVE-2023-44487", "in_kev": true, "severity": "High", "published": "2023-10-10T14:15:10.883000+05:30", "cvss_score": 7.5, "epss_score": 0.944, "updated_at": "2025-11-07T19:00:41.810000+05:30", "cvss_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "description": "The HTTP/2 protocol allows a denial of service (server resource consumption) because request cancellation can reset many streams quickly, as exploited in the wild in August through October 2023.", "has_exploit": true, "kev_product": "HTTP/2", "cvss_version": "3.1", "kev_due_date": "2023-10-31", "kev_vuln_name": "HT